        "title": "Evidence",
        "body": "The links a graph holds are found in components/GraphEditor/utils/graphLinks.js: a Page Route’s destination, a node’s link, and the links written in Content. The workspace draws one, from the graph that holds it to the graph it points at, when both are open (components/GraphEditor/utils/workspaceBridge.js), and paints it with this class’s Strokes, route and arrow. An address that names something other than an open graph is not drawn yet.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
